            <ArticleTitle>Teratodermoid mimicking cholecystitis.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>494-8</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1002/ccr3.554</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>An acute abdomen assessment in pregnancy is complicated. Pain can have obstetric and nonobstetric causes. Cholecystitis is a common cause of pain in pregnancy with significant morbidity if not managed promptly. We report a case of a ruptured, torted, right ovarian teratodermoid erroneously diagnosed as cholecystitis in pregnancy.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
